# Change Log
All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.

The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](http://keepachangelog.com/)
and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](http://semver.org/).

## [0.3.0] - 2026-10-03

### Added

* add optional per-block `timeout` and `output_limit` settings
* add regression coverage for independent updates, manual-only intervals, command failures, output limits, and process cleanup
* add GitHub Actions CI for the MSRV and current stable Rust

### Changed

* run blocks independently instead of waiting for an entire batch before publishing
* use monotonic per-block deadlines and skip missed periodic ticks instead of replaying stale work
* coalesce repeated manual hits while a block is running into one follow-up execution
* make zero and omitted intervals manual-only, matching the documented configuration contract
* run commands with null stdin and supervise each invocation as its own process group
* bound captured command output to 64 KiB by default while continuing to drain pipes
* report command failures with block context and bounded stderr without stopping unrelated blocks
* search config locations in precedence order instead of selecting only the first environment-derived path
* improve error messages and expose underlying errors through `std::error::Error::source`

### Fixed

* reject invalid, non-finite, negative, unrepresentable, and empty-command configuration before opening X11
* prevent a slow or stuck block from delaying unrelated block updates
* prevent timer work from accumulating in an unbounded catch-up queue
* terminate and reap ordinary command process groups on SIGINT, SIGTERM, timeout, and fatal runtime failure
* drain X11 hit queues larger than 1,024 IDs without leaving the tail permanently stuck
* deduplicate non-adjacent hit IDs and process a pending hit queue at startup
* treat X11 connection loss as fatal instead of retrying forever without a usable bar
* check X11 subscription and WM_NAME protocol errors instead of discarding nested failures
* keep blocked stdout consumers from stalling the coordinator or growing pending updates without bounds

## [0.2.1] - 226-10-03

### Added

* add `--stdout` output while preserving X11-based manual updates

## [0.2.0] - 2024-02-12

* move x11 stuff and timer for tasks into separate threads

## [0.1.1] - 2024-02-10

* add nix related stuff
* add support of `--version` cli arg


## [0.1.0] - 2024-02-09

Initial version of this project.
